{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system","id":1526980,"title":"[W5] Fixing the caern system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-17T05:57:25-08:00","id":1526980,"title":"[W5] Fixing the caern system","content":"This thread is a spinoff from my <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1525625-w5-fixing-harano-and-hauglosk\">previous thread </a>about house ruling W5. (By the way, in case anyone is interested, you can find the <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/txvo7sxvxfznthk6dyofp/House-Rules-1.5.pdf?rlkey=epywxru9mat8s6rzxanxq8gmg&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">latest version of the house rules</a> [PDF, Dropbox link] here.)<br /> <br /> In this thread, I would like to build on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a>'s cool idea of adapting V5's domain and coterie system to a caern and pack system. I've re-familiarized myself with V5's rules and had a look at my old 1st-W20 books (mainly the rulebooks, <i>Caerns: Places of Power</i>, and <i>Guardians of the Caerns</i>).<br /> <br /> To recap V5's domain and coteries system:<ul><li>Each member of the coterie adds one (or, depending on ST decision, more dots) to the shared coterie pool. In addition, players can decide to put dots from their own advantages pool into the coterie pool. Dots in the coterie pool can be spent on domain or on other advantages/backgrounds/merits that can be used by the whole coterie.</li> <li>Domains are defined by three stats: <b>Chasse</b> (size of the domain), which determines how difficult hunting is (the bigger, the easier); <b>Lien </b>(coterie's integration into the domain), which adds dice to social rolls with people living in the domain; <b>Portillon </b>(security against intrusion or disruption), which reduces dice from enemies' dice pools to intrude or gather intelligence. Chasse is limited to five dots, I couldn't find limits for Lien and Portillon.</li> <li>Coteries are basically group templates that have certain prerequisites (e.g., certain amount of Chasse, Lien, or Portillon dots; certain advantages/backgrounds) and allow the sharing of advantages/backgrounds/merits. In the Players Guide there are specific coterie merits.</li> <li>The Players Guide also expands the domain system by adding merits for Chasse, Lien, and Portillon. These count towards coterie requirements and are basically a bit more flavorful variation of the basic system.</li> </ul>That's it, basically. To my knowledge, there isn't a more abstract system to expand the domain, beyond buying more advantage dots, putting them into the coterie pool, and spending them on the domain (either dots in the three stats or merits), coterie assets, or coterie merits.<br /> <br /> Now, the question is, how could we apply this to W5?<br /> <br /> I think it's safe to assume that instead of Chasse, we can use the caern's power, which influences the difficulty to step sideways. A variation of Lien could add dice to social interactions with spirits, and Portillon could be used as is. So far, so good...<br /> <br /> However, in V5 there is one coterie per domain, so the question is how this should be handled in W5. After all, a septs usually consists of several packs. So, should the pack pools all be pooled together for spending on the caern and the shared advantages/backgrounds/merits? EDIT: Personally, I'm not sure. Adding all the pack pools of several packs together might make it too easy to build very strong caerns. I feel there has to be a point of diminishing returns if you have too many packs in one caern.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Another issue is whether to bring back moon bridges. I'm tending towards yes, but maybe as an additional set of merits, not as something a caern automatically has.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-17-2023, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T14:36:03-08:00","id":1527002,"title":"","content":"Possibly we could work renown into this?<ul><li>The first stat could truly be Power</li> <li>The second could be Renown - which marks how influential and popular you are in the Caern, and you can block levels in this with say total pack renown? This would give them influence, but also block them behind having a Renown total before their influence and control of the Caern can go up?</li> <li>The third one could be Guardians and represent the Spirits, Wardens and packs that are in charge of making sure the Caern is not found and that defenses are ready</li> </ul><br /> I feel Moon Bridges and establishing them is key to actually building the nation and keeping ties between disparate groups together. They are what keeps the culture of the Tribes and the nation together. I'd tie them directly into power, but have their useage locked behind Renown - i.e. a young pack can only use it when directed by an Elder, and a older pack can actually request and or open them on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T22:56:37-08:00","id":1527037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527002#post1527002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly we could work renown into this?<ul><li>The first stat could truly be Power</li> <li>The second could be Renown - which marks how influential and popular you are in the Caern, and you can block levels in this with say total pack renown? This would give them influence, but also block them behind having a Renown total before their influence and control of the Caern can go up?</li> <li>The third one could be Guardians and represent the Spirits, Wardens and packs that are in charge of making sure the Caern is not found and that defenses are ready</li> </ul><br /> I feel Moon Bridges and establishing them is key to actually building the nation and keeping ties between disparate groups together. They are what keeps the culture of the Tribes and the nation together. I'd tie them directly into power, but have their useage locked behind Renown - i.e. a young pack can only use it when directed by an Elder, and a older pack can actually request and or open them on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Renown could definitely play a part concerning the pack system, but I don't see it as something for the caern system. My idea would be to establish the caern system first and, based on that, I can develop the different pack types (with all the associated rules). But I think the idea of pack renown makes sense and has merit to unlock certain benefits, such as access to sept assets or the moon bridge.<br /> <br /> I'm currently in the process of copy-pasting and rewriting a first draft for the caern system. I imagine the steps in the character creation process will be:<br /> 1) Determine Pack Pool<br /> 2) Caern creation<br /> 3) Pack patron creation<br /> 4) Determine pack type<br /> I think I'll write the parts in the same order, so they can properly build on one another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T16:13:50-08:00","id":1527070,"title":"","content":"I will need to find a better moment later to write down all of it but some ideas:<ul><li>Pack-Type is prioritized as it is about what the group does</li> <li>Some Pack-Types are associated with caerns but not all</li> <li>Caerns have their own mini-char-sheet</li> <li>The bigger structure horizontally is Sept and non-Sept/outsider: There's a difference between helping a Sept that protects a caern and dealing with a dormant caern.</li> <li>The inspiration for what Pack-Types do is to emphasize what PCs do. For example, the core-scenario from the W5-corebook of a Pack awakening a caern on their own shouldn't be about raising the caern-level of the thing. Instead that Pack-Type should be about gathering contacts and allies because you build the Sept first and then turn to get the spirit of the caern to grow in power. The idea is that a caern at level 1 is an egg and so the priority is protection.</li> <li>Meanwhile, for Pack-Types serving Septs the Caern starts at five dots (with caerns having a 10 dot rating now) and dealing with the caern's spirit is different. Depending on your Pack-Type serving the caern-spirit might be what you're doing. Something like that.</li> <li>In regards to Pack-Patron-Spirits, rather than making it about buying dots... the whole thing is put on a separate track. Your Pack-Patron-Spirit wants you to act a certain way (within the bounds of what your Pack-Type is) and you accrue specific Pack-Patron-XP that way which you then spend on Pack-Patron specifc benefits. And what I'm thinking of is something along the lines of a Blades in the Dark Crew sheet.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T23:11:14-08:00","id":1527079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527070#post1527070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will need to find a better moment later to write down all of it but some ideas:<ul><li>Pack-Type is prioritized as it is about what the group does</li> <li>Some Pack-Types are associated with caerns but not all</li> <li>Caerns have their own mini-char-sheet</li> <li>The bigger structure horizontally is Sept and non-Sept/outsider: There's a difference between helping a Sept that protects a caern and dealing with a dormant caern.</li> <li>The inspiration for what Pack-Types do is to emphasize what PCs do. For example, the core-scenario from the W5-corebook of a Pack awakening a caern on their own shouldn't be about raising the caern-level of the thing. Instead that Pack-Type should be about gathering contacts and allies because you build the Sept first and then turn to get the spirit of the caern to grow in power. The idea is that a caern at level 1 is an egg and so the priority is protection.</li> <li>Meanwhile, for Pack-Types serving Septs the Caern starts at five dots (with caerns having a 10 dot rating now) and dealing with the caern's spirit is different. Depending on your Pack-Type serving the caern-spirit might be what you're doing. Something like that.</li> <li>In regards to Pack-Patron-Spirits, rather than making it about buying dots... the whole thing is put on a separate track. Your Pack-Patron-Spirit wants you to act a certain way (within the bounds of what your Pack-Type is) and you accrue specific Pack-Patron-XP that way which you then spend on Pack-Patron specifc benefits. And what I'm thinking of is something along the lines of a Blades in the Dark Crew sheet.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll refrain from commenting too much on it before you can elaborate, but I'm not entirely sure yet which function packs would have mechanically in you vision. Like, sure, pack types are what a pack does, but what does that mean mechanically exactly? (Bonus dice to related rolls? WP regen? Shared advantages? etc.)<br /> <br /> Differentiating between sept and non-sept pack types makes sense to me. The question is, how many non-sept pack types do we even have? Looking at V5, a nomad and maybe a fugitive one, but other than that I'm drawing a blank.<br /> <br /> Hm, I'm not familiar with Blades in the Dark (I'm not into PbtA games generally). Not a fan of separate XP trackers, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T16:54:46-08:00","id":1527095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527079#post1527079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll refrain from commenting too much on it before you can elaborate, but I'm not entirely sure yet which function packs would have mechanically in you vision. Like, sure, pack types are what a pack does, but what does that mean mechanically exactly? (Bonus dice to related rolls? WP regen? Shared advantages? etc.)<br /> <br /> Differentiating between sept and non-sept pack types makes sense to me. The question is, how many non-sept pack types do we even have? Looking at V5, a nomad and maybe a fugitive one, but other than that I'm drawing a blank.<br /> <br /> Hm, I'm not familiar with Blades in the Dark (I'm not into PbtA games generally). Not a fan of separate XP trackers, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all very early-stage stuff... So yeah, maybe the exrta XP-tracker isn't a good idea...<br /> <br /> The biggest issue I have for envisioning this is: What do Garou in W5 actually do? I just come back to the introduction where one paragraph ends with &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; and then only a paragraph later the line is &quot;Otherwise, there will be no tomorrow.&quot;. The way I approached this was to try to stay within the limits of W5's design but with something like this, I can just only and give up. It will be interesting to see what Renegade will do with the setting. Especially since Deepest of Wounds was already running at high speed away from the little worldbuilding the W5 corebook did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-19T21:23:44-08:00","id":1527107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527095#post1527095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's all very early-stage stuff... So yeah, maybe the exrta XP-tracker isn't a good idea...<br /> <br /> The biggest issue I have for envisioning this is: What do Garou in W5 actually do? I just come back to the introduction where one paragraph ends with &quot;It's too late to avert the end.&quot; and then only a paragraph later the line is &quot;Otherwise, there will be no tomorrow.&quot;. The way I approached this was to try to stay within the limits of W5's design but with something like this, I can just only and give up. It will be interesting to see what Renegade will do with the setting. Especially since Deepest of Wounds was already running at high speed away from the little worldbuilding the W5 corebook did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that's a very good point, and it hits the heart of W5's problem. However, I wouldn't focus too much on this stuff... it's a waste of time to be honest!<br /> <br /> The main reason we have this problem in the first place is because V5 wanted to be a continuation of the old metaplot. The problem is, the new books never seemed clear on what their respective splat's eschatology is actually supposed to mean: the literal end of the world, the end of an age, or the end of a people (Kindred, Garou)?<br /> <br /> For me, believing in the Apocalypse being inevitable, seems like a direct path towards harano or hauglosk (your/our redefinition at least), because it means throwing down the towel based on anxiety about the future, about an idea what the future might hold, instead of living in the here and now. For me, the lesson should be not to become paralyzed or sidetracked by fear (i.e., the assumption of certain doom), but to act now, even if it's only small steps, because in the end the small steps add up, and the future is decided by the gradual process.<br /> <br /> In that sense, I feel my house-ruled W5 should be focused on what a pack can do here and now, within its own sphere of influence, to do its part in changing the current course. And, sure, if the old approaches weren't effective enough for changing the trend, then it raises the question what new approaches might work better. And for that, we have to define the old approach and possible new approaches first. Since it's a reboot, I feel we are pretty free to decide on the nature of the old approaches and why they didn't work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But the thing is, all this was already in the legacy editions. We already had the various different approaches to tackling the problem. So, W5's spiel about how the young now have to do everything differently seems disingenuous (unless you retcon the old guard being very single-minded). Functionally, to me, it means we don't have to pay attention to the whole Apocalypse business, because it doesn't change what packs do in comparison to older editions. PCs will do the same shit, we've been playing for the past 30 years, because nothing really changed effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-20-2023, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T06:45:35-08:00","id":1527116,"title":"","content":"Okay, my last post is apparently in Approval limbo because I edited it twice...<br /> <br /> Anyway, here is the first draft of the Caern system based on V5's Domain system: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/sipjnbeb4qllppyy6pxh3/House-Rules-Caern-and-Pack-v1.1.pdf?rlkey=pl0ns92glxcup2rwlza8bduho&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Link to PDF (Dropbox)</a><br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">EDIT: Slightly updated version.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 12-21-2023, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T01:42:27-08:00","id":1527145,"title":"","content":"Okay, I added two more Wards Merit that'll be included in the next update:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Gallain Watchmen (</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\"> to </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The caern\u2019s bawn houses a group of Gallain who have organized a private militia to protect the area. Each dot of Gallain Watchmen supplies four Average guards and one Gifted boss (see <i>Supporting Character Templates</i>, p. 102). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Warding Glyphs (</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\"> to </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> Power \u2022\u2022 or more; Wards \u2022\u2022 or more<br /> Along its perimeter, the caern possesses Warding Glyphs barring other supernatural forces. These glyphs cannot be actively deactivated, but the caern\u2019s Rite master may allow individuals to pass. Discuss the limits of the Warding Glyphs with the Storyteller. Choose one type of supernatural creature: fera, vampires, mages, ghosts, fair folk, etc. Each dot of this Merit adds one to the difficulty for this type of supernatural creature to enter or magically scry the premises. This Wards Merits must be bought and increased separately for each type of supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> <br /> =====<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about the Pack Types now. I've come with a few rough ideas:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Caern Guardians (protecting a caern from attack and outside influence)</span></li> <li>Callers of the Wyld (serving the caern's patron spirit and seeing to its needs)</li> <li>Community Builders (influencing human communities, raising awareness)</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hunting Party</span> (hunting down a fugitive enemy)</li> <li>Infiltrators (infiltrating enemy territory to gather intelligence and possibly assassinate)</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Investigators</span> (investigate the Wyrm's influence and identify targets for attack)</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monkey Wrenchers / Saboteurs</span>\u200b (sabotage enemy infrastructure or operations)</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sept Envoys</span>\u200b (improve diplomatic relations with other septs and caerns)</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit Questers</span> (uncover hidden knowledge or find allies in the spirit world)</li> <li>Strike Force (attack specific targets, usually based on the information from other pack types or the Wyrm Foe)</li> <li>Truthcatchers (investigate and settle disputes among the members of the sept)</li> <li>Urrah Troubleshooter (keeping trouble away from the Garou from humans and keeping up the Veil)</li> </ul>\u200bFor non-sept pack types:<ul><li>Nomads (traveling packs without association to a sept, trying to survive)</li> <li>Fugitives (hunted, justly or unjustly, by their former allies)</li> </ul><br /> Do you have other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:40:53-08:00","id":1527168,"title":"","content":"A couple of ideas:<br /> <br /> For non-Sept-Packs:<ul><li>Don't know what a good name would be but it's the main-scenario of the book: You have a Pack that finds a dormant or lost caern and reawakens it. But instead of the focus being on the caern itself, the focus is on gathering allies and contacts both in the physical realm and in the Umbra. Instead of just buffing the caern, the group-dynamic is more about populating a new Sept. So, the caern-spirit is weak compared to the kind of spirit &quot;Callers of the Wyld&quot; deal with and instead things like the Amenity &quot;Kin-Beacon&quot; and dots in Allies and Contacts are emphasized.</li> <li>Umbral hunters: The idea is that this is the Pack-Type for when you want to go full-fantasy and have PCs spend more time in the Umbra than in physical space. Another idea I had is if that Pack-type has a close relationship with Starving Remnants as in them having Rites that keep these Packs from becoming them and maybe there are sacred hunts where the Pack competes with Starving Remnants and allows them to either &quot;move on&quot;, turn into a friendly Spirit (they find their own niche of existence within the Umbra) or if the change happened only recently, they can be returned to their physical state.</li> <li>A wandering Pack of storytellers and lorekeepers (with a lot of Silent Strider members naturally) that go from Sept to Sept. (Hmm, it's probably more like a more Garou-ish interpretation of the Nomad-template, I guess)</li> </ul>Unrelated other ideas:<ul><li>What do you think of the idea of turning the Pack-Patron-Spirit into a Loresheet? I would have to take a look at all the Loresheets whether there's a way to streamline the process of creating one, so people can have their custom Pack-Patron-Spirits. But for established Patron-Spirits from previous editions, it should be easy to come up with five dots of benefits that fit the writing.</li> <li>I also think one system that W5 needs is a way to deal with investigating Spirits. Wyrm-sense was removed so you can't tell the difference between whether a disease-spirit is of the Wyld or the Wyrm. The book has that part but the part where now Garou are supposed to investigate Spirits first to figure out what the deal is needs a system. I think the Project-system from the V5 corebook and the V5 Players Guide could be repurposed for this. Just as a way of allowing a group to &quot;zoom out&quot; while dealing with a Spirit. That allows STs to make Spirits a more general phenomenon and not having every Spirit be there for important narrative roles like antagonist, ally or whatever. You can just have spiritual activity and if a player cares about it, you have a quick system to abstractly resolve the process of engaging with the Spirit and if nobody cares... well, that's that. But that way an ST can promote engaging with the Umbra and Spirits more.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T21:25:08-08:00","id":1527222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527168#post1527168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of ideas:<br /> <br /> For non-Sept-Packs:<ul><li>Don't know what a good name would be but it's the main-scenario of the book: You have a Pack that finds a dormant or lost caern and reawakens it. But instead of the focus being on the caern itself, the focus is on gathering allies and contacts both in the physical realm and in the Umbra. Instead of just buffing the caern, the group-dynamic is more about populating a new Sept. So, the caern-spirit is weak compared to the kind of spirit &quot;Callers of the Wyld&quot; deal with and instead things like the Amenity &quot;Kin-Beacon&quot; and dots in Allies and Contacts are emphasized.</li> <li>Umbral hunters: The idea is that this is the Pack-Type for when you want to go full-fantasy and have PCs spend more time in the Umbra than in physical space. Another idea I had is if that Pack-type has a close relationship with Starving Remnants as in them having Rites that keep these Packs from becoming them and maybe there are sacred hunts where the Pack competes with Starving Remnants and allows them to either &quot;move on&quot;, turn into a friendly Spirit (they find their own niche of existence within the Umbra) or if the change happened only recently, they can be returned to their physical state.</li> <li>A wandering Pack of storytellers and lorekeepers (with a lot of Silent Strider members naturally) that go from Sept to Sept. (Hmm, it's probably more like a more Garou-ish interpretation of the Nomad-template, I guess)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Great ideas, I'll try to integrate them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527168#post1527168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated other ideas:<ul><li>What do you think of the idea of turning the Pack-Patron-Spirit into a Loresheet? I would have to take a look at all the Loresheets whether there's a way to streamline the process of creating one, so people can have their custom Pack-Patron-Spirits. But for established Patron-Spirits from previous editions, it should be easy to come up with five dots of benefits that fit the writing.</li> <li>I also think one system that W5 needs is a way to deal with investigating Spirits. Wyrm-sense was removed so you can't tell the difference between whether a disease-spirit is of the Wyld or the Wyrm. The book has that part but the part where now Garou are supposed to investigate Spirits first to figure out what the deal is needs a system. I think the Project-system from the V5 corebook and the V5 Players Guide could be repurposed for this. Just as a way of allowing a group to &quot;zoom out&quot; while dealing with a Spirit. That allows STs to make Spirits a more general phenomenon and not having every Spirit be there for important narrative roles like antagonist, ally or whatever. You can just have spiritual activity and if a player cares about it, you have a quick system to abstractly resolve the process of engaging with the Spirit and if nobody cares... well, that's that. But that way an ST can promote engaging with the Umbra and Spirits more.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, my problem with the Pack Patron as Loresheet is twofold: First, Loresheets are optional, and I like the idea that every pack has its own patron spirit. Second, having written a few homebrew Loresheets for V5 myself, I really don't know whether a Pack Patron would offer enough meat (so to speak) for having five distinct Merits of different power level. I mean, I'm open for it, but I don't see the advantage currently.<br /> <br /> Re: Investigating spirits: That's a very good point... I should look at the project system again. Thanks for that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T21:47:11-08:00","id":1527223,"title":"","content":"By the way, I restructured the house rules document, gave it a cover (admittedly AI-generated), and put everything together. That's everything I got at the moment.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/1iwo9lwkg5jpqffyv2x4r/House-Rules-v2.pdf?rlkey=yja71epe2goeelq4xyalgbik9&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">New document (PDF, Dropbox).</a></b><br /> <br /> I'm going on Xmas vacation today, so hopefully, I'll manage to write something for the pack types in the next days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T00:38:41-08:00","id":1527484,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm currently writing the pack types and I need your help. I'm currently surrounded by my whole extended family and currently have little capacity for the rules bits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It would be a great help if you could suggest appropriate <b>Prerequisites </b>(including the caern's Power, Harmony and Wards rating), <b>Possible Extras </b>and share your ideas for possible <b>Common Pack Advantages</b> and <b>Flaws</b> (like Coterie Advantages and Flaws in the <i>V5 Players Guide</i>). Thanks in advance!<br /> <br /> Here's the first batch:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Caern Guardians</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">The pack has been chosen by the Warder, the sept\u2019s chief guardian, to protect the caern and its bawn from outside attacks and influence. Guardians are loyal to the Warder and are obliged to follow their orders over any given by other sept officials. They often receive powerful talismans to aid in their tasks and hold a place of honor within the sept. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Callers of the Wyld</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Members of this pack are tasked with attending to the needs of the caern\u2019s patron spirit. They keep up the good relationship between the patron spirit and the sept by performing the necessary propitiatory rituals, listening (and sometimes deciphering) the patron spirit\u2019s wishes and demands, and fulfilling whatever tasks it gives them. When the caern\u2019s patron spirit is content, the caern and the sept can better harmonize, allowing both to grow stronger and more united.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Community Builders</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Realizing how intricately Garou are connected with wolves and humans, more and more packs of Community Builders have formed in recent decades. These pack usually focus on building sustainable communities and networks to protect and preserve wolf populations, to educate the human public about the importance of wolves to their respective ecosystems, and to raise awareness about environmental issues. Some Community Builders also work hard with human activists to lobby for more environmental protection laws in order to tackle systemic imbalances of power that favor the Wyrm. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Ghost Healer</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">These packs specialize on rescuing, redeeming, or in some cases hunt Starving Remnants. When there are signs of a Starving Remnant haunting the Spirit Wilds near the caern, Ghost Healers search for the lost spirit. Sometimes they find a newly lost Garou whose physical state can still be restored. Often, Ghost Healers are too late unfortunately. In these cases, they try helping the Starving Remnant to \u201cmove on\u201d by teaching them to control their Rage, thus ending their confusion and allowing them to find their own niche as local spirits. In more difficult cases, the Ghost Healers perform a dangerous, but sacred hunt chasing the Starving Remnant deep into the Umbra. There, in a mysterious spirit wilderness called the Eternal Hunting Grounds, the Starving Remnant transforms into a wolf-shaped hunter spirit and becomes a naturalized part of the spiritscape. Only if a Starving Remnant is too malicious and dangerous to be kept alive, Ghost Healers hunt it down and destroy it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Hunting Party</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">These packs locate, stalk, hunt down, and kill specific targets, usually by order of the sept\u2019s Council of Elders or its Wyrm Foe, who coordinates the sept\u2019s packs and plans strikes against the sept\u2019s enemies. The targets are usually servants of the Wyrm, but they can also be dangerous humans, fugitive Garou, local vampires, or rarely even rogue spirits.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Infiltrators</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Hunting Parties and Strike Forces can only do a good job, if their intelligence is accurate enough. Infiltrator packs are tasked to enter enemy territory or to embed themselves in enemy organizations in order to gather such intelligence. Rarely, when aiming at a high-ranking target that is too difficult to eliminate for \u201coutside\u201d packs, Infiltrators assassinate the target from within, often burning their cover in the process. It is no secret that Infiltrators have one of the most important and dangerous jobs in a sept, yet are often eyed with great suspicion by the sept\u2019s more conservative elements.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Investigators</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">While Infiltrator packs work behind the enemy\u2019s lines to provide crucial intelligence, Investigators packs do the hard legwork from the outside to uncover the Wyrm\u2019s influence and to identify vital targets. Often, these packs have good contacts among journalists, watchdog organizations, and law enforcement agencies in order to always keep an ear to the ground about where the servants of the Wyrm will spread their corruption next. As soon as a viable target is identified, Investigator packs usually brief the assault packs and coordinate their attacks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Druk Text Bold Trial\"><span style=\"color:#496e43\">Monkeywrenchers</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:IBM Plex Sans\">Monkeywrencher packs specialize on sabotaging the enemy\u2019s infrastructure and operations. While this often means directly shutting down Pentex factories, burning down secret laboratories, or destroying logging equipment, more urban packs also hack enemy computer systems and infest them with Weaver-infused viruses or sabotage a company\u2019s value on the stock market. Both Monkeywrenchers and Infiltrators work covertly, but the former tend to be more offensive and take a more hands-on approach, whereas Infiltrators usually stick to subtle intelligence-gathering in order to avoid raising suspicion.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T03:16:41-08:00","id":1527488,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm swamped by all the Christmas family stuff as well. Not a lot of opportunities to sit down and figure this stuff out. lol<br /> <br /> BTW , I did think of another non-Sept Pack-Type. It only gets a tiny sidebar in the book but as a W5 idea, it's worth a mention: Moon Cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T05:15:38-08:00","id":1527491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527488#post1527488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm swamped by all the Christmas family stuff as well. Not a lot of opportunities to sit down and figure this stuff out. lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I sympathize! lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527488#post1527488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW , I did think of another non-Sept Pack-Type. It only gets a tiny sidebar in the book but as a W5 idea, it's worth a mention: Moon Cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, excellent idea!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T07:35:01-08:00","id":1527691,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/r0kc305rx1g6pznjmbjxs/House-Rules-v3.1.pdf?rlkey=673lqb88wuqeqkzhumabmc6rv&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\"><b>It is done...</b> </a>(For those of you who are still interested.)<br /> <br /> It is too much to post it outside the PDF (overall 38 pages!), but I finished the caern creation system with caern traits and respective merits and flaws, pack merits and flaws, pack types (20 different types, I think), and so on.<br /> <br /> I also included the streamlined project rules from the V5 Players Guide for uncovering the Wyrm's influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":".  Updated with some fixes 01-03-2024, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T13:34:40-08:00","id":1527946,"title":"","content":"Consider posting this to STV. You would be the first to publish a w5 supplement and maybe you can get a few bucks out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T14:35:48-08:00","id":1527955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526980-w5-fixing-the-caern-system?p=1527946#post1527946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider posting this to STV. You would be the first to publish a w5 supplement and maybe you can get a few bucks out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the suggestion, but I prefer to keep it strictly as a personal project that I happen to share in order to get feedback from the fan community. In order to properly publish it, I'd have to rewrite it, since I copied various parts from W5 or older WtA publications (like the renown stuff), changing only bits or expanding it as necessary. Also, I didn't really innovate anything, I just repurposed stuff that has already been published. It would feel wrong to sell or even publish it under my name, so to speak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T09:12:24-08:00","id":1528216,"title":"","content":"I commissioned MrGone to create/adapt sheets for my house rules. He's currently working on the Garou sheet, but here's a sheet for the Gallain (basically, a Mortals sheet in W5 design):<br /> <br /> 1-page: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/wpgyvm3srf4nl8aepkkry/Werewolf_5thEdition_1-Page_Gallain_Interactive.pdf?rlkey=uodqmcjtcfqt4so4a4lw5upp9&amp;dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/wpgyvm3srf4nl8aepkkry/Werewolf_5thEdition_1-Page_Gallain_Interactive.pdf?rlkey=uodqmcjtcfqt4so 4a4lw5upp9&amp;dl=0</a><br /> 2-page: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/bwvxpozhplqh03q17bv82/Werewolf_5thEdition_2-Pa